A new sky, new clouds and better light for Far Cry 2, from sunrise through storms to the middle of the night.

[size=4][b]What it changes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The sky[/b] follows the sun: deep blue at noon, orange and purple sunsets, and stars all night.[/*]
[*][b]Real clouds[/b], lit by the sun, with thin high clouds and plane trails above them. They move with the game's clock, so a loaded save shows the sky you left.[/*]
[*][b]Storms[/b] bring thick clouds and grey light, without the land vanishing into fog.[/*]
[*][b]Clear days look clear[/b]: a blue sky instead of a washed-out white one, and shade you can see into.[/*]
[*][b]The sun[/b] throws light shafts past the clouds, and its glare only blinds you when you look straight at it.[/*]
[*][b]Shadows[/b]: clouds shade the ground as they pass, and sun shadows reach further and stop flickering on buildings.[/*]
[*][b]Grass, leaves and rocks[/b] catch the sun properly. Grass and leaves glow with the sun behind them, rocks look like stone.[/*]
[*][b]Nights[/b] are darker, with a smaller moon whose light casts shadows. Colours fade in the dark, while fires and lamps stay bright.[/*]
[*][b]No more yellow tint[/b] over everything, and a faint film grain.[/*]
[*][b]Ambient occlusion[/b]: corners and creases go darker. Off by default.[/*]
[/list]

Every part can be switched on or off in the game: [b]Options → Mod Configuration Menu[/b].

[b]Coming from 1.1.0 or older?[/b] Delete [b]bin\sky-overhaul.ini[/b] once, or the new look won't fully take effect.

[size=4][b]How to install (Vortex)[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/about/vortex/]Vortex[/url] and its Far Cry 2 extension.[/*]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] on this page and enable the mod. Vortex also offers to get [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], which this mod needs.[/*]
[*]Start the game with the [b]Play[/b] button in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
Not using Vortex? Install it with JackAll instead, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Needs Far Cry 2 patch 1.03[/b], Steam or GOG, and FCSE 1.4.0 or later.[/*]
[*][b]Turn Bloom on[/b] in Options → Video, or the sun is a flat disc.[/*]
[*][b]Cloud shadows need Depth pass quality on High[/b] or above. Everything else works without it.[/*]
[*][b]Doesn't mix with other lighting, fog or weather mods.[/b] Whichever loads last wins.[/*]
[*][b]Known issue:[/b] colours also fade in the dark indoors at night.[/*]
[/list]

